.TH elfshaker-esi-remove 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-esi\-remove \- Removes pack URLs from one or more ESI indexes
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker esi remove\fR [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-backup\fR] [\fB\-\-also\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIesi_file\fR> <\fIpack_url\fR>... 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Removes pack URLs from one or more ESI indexes
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Ignore stored URLs that are not present.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-backup\fR
Do not replace <ESI_FILE>.bak with the previous contents.
.TP
\fB\-\-also\fR \fI<ESI_FILE>\fR
Apply the operation to another ESI file; may be repeated.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show informational progress and diagnostic messages.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Use PATH as the data directory containing packs, indexes, loose objects, remotes, and HEAD. This does not change the working directory.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIesi_file\fR>
Primary ESI file to edit.
.TP
<\fIpack_url\fR>...
Stored pack URLs to remove.
